  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 8 - Arithmetic Operator
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_arithmetic_operators
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Arithmetic Operators
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Arithmetic Operators are symbols used to perform calculations on
    values.\r\n\nCommon arithmetic operators:\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>+
    </color></font> \u2192 addition\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>-
    </color></font> \u2192 subtraction\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>*
    </color></font> \u2192 multiplication\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>/
    </color></font> \u2192 division\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>%
    </color></font> \u2192 modulo (remainder)\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>//</color></font>
    \u2192 floor division\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>**</color></font>
    \u2192 exponent\r\n\nParentheses can be used to control calculation order: Example:
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>(</color><color=#B5CEA8>10</color>
    <color=#D4D4D4>+</color> <color=#B5CEA8>8</color><color=#D4D4D4>)</color> <color=#D4D4D4>*</color>
    <color=#B5CEA8>2</color></font>\r\nThis ensures the addition happens first. Result:
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#B5CEA8>36</color></font>\r\n\nThe <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#D4D4D4>+</color></font> operator can also combine text (string
    values). Example: <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"Hello \"</color>
    <color=#D4D4D4>+</color> <color=#CE9178>\"Robot\"</color></font>\nResult: <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"Hello Robot\"</color></font>"
  isImageBig: 0
